From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:30:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] MTP first form: G6_MTP_LASTROW=1 routes only each
 session's last row through layer 78's experts (default off)

A first-form draft step of a+1 rows exists to write layer 78's caches for rows 0..a-1; only the last row's
token, log-probability and hidden are read. The caches are written in the attention block from the layer
input, before the MoE, so the other rows' routed experts are skipped: k_router_plan takes a keep mask
(by value on the solo graphs, from S2In on the S2 path via k_s2_last_rows) and gives the other rows no slot.
A routed row's K1 bytes do not depend on the other rows' routes (the S2 A1 property), so the caches and the
last row are the bytes of the full step. In the S2 runtime signature.

Tests: kernels/tests/mtp_lastrow_test.cu (synthetic exlr8 v2 layer, one GB10: kept rows byte for byte vs the
full plan, fuse 0/1, ROUTE_OVL 0/1/2, plain and graph, M 1..32; bench of the saving); m4sim
G6_MTP_LASTROW_CHECK=1 + scripts/mtp_lastrow_check.sh (caches, last rows, every target line, flag off vs on).
